WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.536
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.604
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:08.107
Well, guys, I hope everyone's
doing a little better

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:10.577
after last night's
presidential debate.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:13.179
My only wish for tonight
is that you laugh at these jokes

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.949
as much as Joe Biden
laughed at President Trump.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:18.184
[ Biden laughing ]

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.654
-What about those questions?
-I will say...

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:22.689
-Less than -- Sir --

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.625
[ Imitating Biden laughter ]

00:00:28.193 --> 00:00:30.763
[ Laughing rhythmically ]

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:36.236
♪♪

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:42.175
After last night's disaster,
Trump and Biden both confirmed

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.410
they will appear
at the next debate.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.212
Meanwhile, Americans were like,

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.281
"Yeah, you guys
have fun with that."

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.649
I can't believe
there's two more of these.

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:53.319
It's like getting
food poisoning at Chipotle

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:56.823
then trying to clean out
your system with more Chipotle.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.958
The reviews of last night's
debate are in,

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.559
and here's what the media
had to say.

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:02.195
-This was the most chaotic

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.363
presidential debate
I've ever seen.

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:06.766
-What happened on that debate
stage was unlike anything

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.668
that has ever happened on
a presidential debate stage.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:11.170
-That was a hot mess

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.940
inside a dumpster fire
inside a train wreck.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.110
-It was undignified at many
times. It was cringeworthy.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.979
-I'm at a bit of
a loss for words here

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.847
to describe
what we've just witnessed.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:23.616
-That was a [bleep] show.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.051
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.187
-It's not a good sign
when the presidential debate

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.155
gets the same reviews as "Cats."

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.391
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:35.595
Seriously, it was like watching
"The View" on bath salts.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:38.498
It was like watching a debate
between two deejay air horns.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:41.935
[ Rasta air horns blaring ]

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.103
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:45.638
It was a lot to stomach.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:47.106
If the debate aired on Netflix,

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:48.774
they would have had
a popup that asked,

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:51.411
"How are you still watching?"

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.680
All this morning's headlines

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.149
were about what a disaster
the debate was.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.217
Like, the "New York Post"
headline said

00:01:58.217 --> 00:01:59.952
"A Hot Mess of a Debate."

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:03.022
Or a "Washington Post" one
that said "Trump Sets The Tone

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:06.058
For The Worst Presidential
Debate In Living Memory."

00:02:06.058 --> 00:02:07.827
And this headline said

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.195
"Millions Stay Up Till 4AM

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.230
Googling
'How Do I Move To Canada?'"

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.798
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:17.770
This one said
"Dew Garita Stock Up 75%."

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.705
And finally
this last headline says

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:22.475
"Priests seen yelling,
'Yes, today, Satan.'"

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.577
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.479
[ Applause ]

00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:32.251
[ Laughs ]

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.887
"Yes, today, Satan."

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:36.990
Oh. The debate was crazy.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.125
Some people compared it
to a circus.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:41.494
And get this -- during CNN's
post-debate coverage,

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:45.197
Van Jones shared a message
from actual circus workers.

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:47.233
-Circus workers actually
reached out to my team.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.269
They say, "Actually,
we take offense.

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:51.337
We are careful
and respectful people,

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.372
and we work
very carefully together."

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:55.474
So the circus workers
are taking offense

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.143
that this was worse
than a circus.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:59.979
-Yeah.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.148
Clowns don't want
to be compared to Trump.

00:03:03.148 --> 00:03:05.217
They were like, "Sure,
we both wear a lot of makeup,

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:08.788
but we pay way more in taxes."

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.456
You know it's a crazy night
when a guy on CNN

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.957
very seriously says,

00:03:11.957 --> 00:03:14.494
"I've just received a message
from some circus workers and...

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:18.764
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:20.733
...they're not pleased."

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.969
Of course, one of
the biggest moments

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:25.104
that everyone's
still talking about

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:27.840
is when Trump failed
to condemn white supremacists

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.810
and instead told them
to "stand back and stand by."

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.079
Here are some reactions
to that comment.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:35.148
-It was really a sad night
for our country

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:38.017
in that the President
of the United States

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:41.588
would not dissociate himself
from white supremacists.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.231
-Donald Trump
blew the biggest layup

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.133
in the history of debates
by saying --

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.135
not condemning
white supremacists.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.370
-Yeah, it's not good
when you ask the President

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.039
if he'll condemn
white supremacy,

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.074
and the "Jeopardy!" music
starts playing in his head

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:03.642
while he thinks it over.

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:05.678
[ "Final Jeopardy!"
theme plays ]

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:11.684
♪♪

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:17.690
♪♪

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.459
[ Theme ends ]

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:20.726
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:22.795
Thank you. That was my
"Jeopardy!" space work.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.263
I can do other --
-Hey!

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:26.399
-Thank you very much.
-You pay for it.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.634
-I know, yeah.
I do other game shows.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:32.271
I do whatever you guys want.
I do birthday parties.

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:34.874
If your kid likes a certain
game show, I'll do that.

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:37.476
You know, space work.
I don't bring any props.

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:42.248
I let the kid imagine
where I am, what I'm holding.

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.749
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.749 --> 00:04:45.785
Could be a light pen.
Could be, you know, a buzzer.

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:48.420
Could be --
It's just a lot of fun.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.089
[ "Final Jeopardy!"
theme plays ]

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:52.024
-No, no, please, I can't do it.
Not now. I'm too busy.

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:54.359
My wife and kids are here.
Don't make me do it.

00:04:54.359 --> 00:04:56.962
-Do it!
-Don't make me do it.

00:04:56.962 --> 00:04:59.365
I just don't --
-Do it!

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:02.435
[ "Final Jeopardy!"
theme plays ]

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:10.409
♪♪

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:11.577
[ Theme fades out ]

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.078
[ Applause ]
-Wait. Please.

00:05:13.078 --> 00:05:15.848
I'm trying to eat my dinner.
I'm trying to eat my dinner.

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:18.150
-On that one, it looked like
you were doing math, though.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.586
-Yeah, I was. That's correct.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:23.389
That's what -- That's
the whole fun of it, yeah.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.424
I let you have your own
adventure, you know?

00:05:25.424 --> 00:05:28.994
-Yeah.
-You're welcome.

00:05:28.994 --> 00:05:31.064
-The Human Escape Room.
-Yeah.

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:32.598
-Love it.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.701
-Are you talking about my brain?

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.404
It's like a Human Escape Room,
yeah, trying to get out.

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:40.539
I saw that this morning
"Fox &amp; Friends"

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:43.242
tried offering Trump some tips
for the next debate.

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:44.910
Check out how they did it.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.913
-Here's my advice for the
President on the next debate.

00:05:47.913 --> 00:05:50.516
One, interrupt less.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:53.852
Two, let Biden flail around.

00:05:53.852 --> 00:05:56.155
And, three, sum it up.

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:58.991
-"Fox &amp; Friends"
is just slowly turning into

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:02.161
"Sesame Street" for Trump.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.930
[As Trump] "Loaf of bread,
container of milk,

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.232
stick of butter.

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:11.336
Loaf of bread, container
of milk, stick of butter.

00:06:11.336 --> 00:06:13.205
Loaf of bread."

00:06:13.205 --> 00:06:15.007
[Normal voice]
And, finally, this isn't good.

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:17.743
I read that more people
are experiencing cracked teeth.

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:20.012
They're experiencing
cracked teeth, and the reason

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.580
is pretty interesting.
Take a look.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:24.449
-One dentist says that
he's seeing five or ten times

00:06:24.449 --> 00:06:26.451
more cracked teeth a day.

00:06:26.451 --> 00:06:29.288
That's what's happening
with stress in the pandemic.

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:30.790
Anxiety can cause you to clench

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.992
or grind your teeth more
at night,

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:36.128
and that in turn
can cause your teeth to crack.

00:06:36.128 --> 00:06:39.232
-Man, oh, man. In 2020,
even our teeth are divided.

